::SPEECH_U03_L07_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: SPEECH_U03_L07_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.01
Question:
In persuasive speech planning, which choice best demonstrates integrated argument skill for situation
{
~A. Use a louder voice so the audience agrees#This confuses delivery volume with persuasive planning. A strong speech still needs a clear claim, evidence, reasoning, and audience awareness.
=B. Use a clear claim with relevant evidence and explained reasoning#Correct. This answer directly supports the lesson skill by using the standard to make communication clearer, better supported, and more audience aware.
~C. Choose details because they sound interesting#Interesting details are not enough. Evidence and examples must connect directly to the claim, purpose, audience, or rebuttal.
~D. Make a personal attack against the opposing speaker#Personal attacks weaken credibility. Persuasive speakers should respond to ideas with evidence and respectful reasoning.
}
::SPEECH_U03_L07_Quiz_Q02::
Question ID: SPEECH_U03_L07_Quiz_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.LST.04
Question:
In persuasive speech planning, which choice best demonstrates integrated argument skill for situation
{
~A. Use a louder voice so the audience agrees#This confuses delivery volume with persuasive planning. A strong speech still needs a clear claim, evidence, reasoning, and audience awareness.
~B. Ignore the opposing view and repeat the claim#This avoids comparison and weakens credibility. Persuasive communication should address opposing views respectfully and explain reasoning.
~C. Choose details because they sound interesting#Interesting details are not enough. Evidence and examples must connect directly to the claim, purpose, audience, or rebuttal.
=D. Address the audience with respectful tone and purposeful support#Correct. This answer directly supports the lesson skill by using the standard to make communication clearer, better supported, and more audience aware.
}
::SPEECH_U03_L07_Quiz_Q03::
Question ID: SPEECH_U03_L07_Quiz_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.LST.03
Question:
In persuasive speech planning, which choice best demonstrates integrated argument skill for situation
{
=A. Compare the opposing view fairly before giving a rebuttal#Correct. This answer directly supports the lesson skill by using the standard to make communication clearer, better supported, and more audience aware.
~B. Ignore the opposing view and repeat the claim#This avoids comparison and weakens credibility. Persuasive communication should address opposing views respectfully and explain reasoning.
~C. Choose details because they sound interesting#Interesting details are not enough. Evidence and examples must connect directly to the claim, purpose, audience, or rebuttal.
~D. Make a personal attack against the opposing speaker#Personal attacks weaken credibility. Persuasive speakers should respond to ideas with evidence and respectful reasoning.
}
